        "original_id": "9233cc94-bb0d-5f36-8eba-d3ebd53ee7ad",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alan Schechter, Hillary Rodham, Susan Estrich, Saul Alinsky\n- Organizations: Wellesley College\n- Works: The Case for Hillary Clinton, “There Is Only the Fight . . . : An Analysis of the Alinsky Model”\n- Roles: advisor, thesis supervisor, professor, community organizer\n\nFacts:\n- In 1969, Hillary Rodham wrote a 92-page senior thesis at Wellesley College about community organizer Saul Alinsky titled “There Is Only the Fight . . . : An Analysis of the Alinsky Model.”\n- During her years at Wellesley College, Alan Schechter served as Hillary Rodham’s advisor and supervised her senior thesis.\n- Susan Estrich’s book The Case for Hillary Clinton says that Hillary Rodham also wrote an honors thesis for Professor Alan Schechter at a different time.",
